# Problem APEX 1.3.36

DOCUMENT();

# Load whatever macros you need for the problem
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric");
$a = random(1, 10, 1);
#$b=random(-7,7,2);
$b = Compute("2*$a");
$c = Compute("$b*$a - $a**2");

$amin = Compute("$a - 2");
$amax = Compute("$a + 2");
$ans  = Compute("$a**2");

BEGIN_PGML
Use the Squeeze Theorem to evaluate the limit 
[`` \lim_{x\to [$a]} f(x) ``]
if
[```
  [$b] x - [$c] \leq f(x) \leq x^2 
```]
on the interval [`[[$amin], [$amax]]`].

[`` \lim_{x\to [$a]} f(x) = ``] [_]{$ans}{10}

Enter *DNE* if the limit does not exist.

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Since 
[```
  \lim_{x \to [$a]} ([$b] x - [$c]) = [$b]([$a]) - [$c] = [$ans] 
```] and 
[```
  \lim_{x \to [$a]} x^2 = ([$a])^2 = [$ans],
```]
by the Squeeze Theorem it must also be true that 
[``` 
    \lim_{x\to [$a]} f(x) = [$ans].
```] 
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();

